    "blurb": "The Fox Theatre show is driven by a monster Playing‑In‑The‑Band sandwich that morphs into an extended Dark Star → Morning Dew climax. Highlights include a searing China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, Bird Song and Phil’s bass fireworks throughout.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Fox Theatre on October 18‑1972 is a high‑octane snapshot of the band in top form. The first set rolls through classic ’72 material—Bertha, Me And My Uncle, Brown Eyed Women—and builds momentum into a crisp China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that showcases Keith’s bright keyboard voice and Bob’s pleasantly gritty rhythm chops. The second set launches with a thunderous Playing In The Band sandwich; the ensuing drum solo segues into a soaring Dark Star that swells into an emotional Morning Dew before snapping back to Playing In The Band for a satisfying close. Phil’s bass is front‑and‑center, delivering a “bombing” solo in Dark Star and a telepathic dialogue with Jerry’s lead lines throughout. Bob’s guitar sits forward in the mix, adding bite and character, while Bill drives the groove with ferocious energy. The recording quality across all six soundboards is uniformly good to excellent, with the Miller SBD (gd1972-10-18.132378.sbd.miller.flac16) offering crystal‑clear separation and minimal hiss, making it the optimal source for this legendary performance.",
